ESINOS:Irene Gonzalo Montesinos is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. She is affiliated with Hospital Infanta Elena in Valdemoro, Madrid, as well as with Hospital Universitario Infanta Elena and Fundación Jiménez Díaz, both located in Madrid.", "HOSPITAL GENERAL DE VILLALBA:The Hospital General de Villalba is a medical institution located in Madrid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. It is noted for its focus on these areas of healthcare, providing specialized services to patients. Nuria Gil Fournier is one of the professionals working at this hospital, contributing to its mission in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition.", "HOSPITAL GENERAL LA MANCHA CENTRO:Hospital General La Mancha Centro is a hospital located in Alcázar de San Juan, Ciudad Real, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.", "HOSPITAL INFANTA ELENA:Hospital Infanta Elena is a hospital located in Valdemoro, Madrid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.", "DIARREA Y ESTREÑIMIENTO:Diarrea y estreñimiento are gastrointestinal symptoms that signify potential underlying structural or functional alterations within the digestive system. These conditions are often discussed in the context of nutrition pathology, highlighting their significance in understanding digestive health. Additionally, the topic of diarrea y estreñimiento is closely related to the role of probiotics and prebiotics in promoting gut health, suggesting that these beneficial microorganisms may play a crucial role in managing and alleviating these symptoms.", "UROLOGY:Urology is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on the field of urology and related topics.", "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF KIDNEY DISEASES:The American Journal of Kidney Diseases is a peer-reviewed journal that focuses on research related to kidney disease and its management.", "HYPEROXALURIA:Hyperoxaluria is a condition characterized by excessive oxalate in the urine, which can lead to kidney stones and other complications.", "NUTRITION PATHOLOGY:Nutrition pathology refers to the study of how nutritional factors contribute to disease processes and health outcomes.", "HUMAN MICROBIOME PROJECT:The Human Microbiome Project is a research initiative launched in 2008, focused on understanding the role of the human microbiome in health and disease. This project aims to characterize the human microbiome through the application of modern genetic techniques, providing insights into how these microbial communities influence various aspects of human health."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}